WEBVTT

00:00.160 --> 00:01.560
Xie Xuan

00:01.640 --> 00:02.720
You lead a unit

00:02.800 --> 00:03.680
Follow me down

00:03.760 --> 00:05.640
To welcome the volunteers into the city

00:05.720 --> 00:07.520
Your general receives orders

00:09.560 --> 00:10.360
Yuanzhi

00:10.440 --> 00:11.160
Here

00:11.240 --> 00:12.907
Send people to the north

00:13.000 --> 00:15.000
To watch for Wunu movements

00:15.080 --> 00:15.360
Your subject

00:15.520 --> 00:16.920
Receives orders

00:32.760 --> 00:34.760
Pay respects to you, sir

00:35.120 --> 00:36.920
Rise, rise

00:41.500 --> 00:45.000
That evening, you hosted a banquet to entertain the volunteers.

00:45.500 --> 00:51.500
However, the volunteer troops were a motley crew, with some having backgrounds as bandits. Whether driven by fiery tempers or provoked by Wunu spies instigating trouble from within...

00:52.000 --> 00:57.500
Several internal factions, disputing over living quarters, escalated from verbal squabbles into armed brawls, and thereafter attempted to abandon the city in anger.

00:58.000 --> 01:03.000
Zhu Yuanzhi refused to open the city gates, drawing the garrison into the vortex of conflict as well, and the situation spiraled completely out of control.

01:03.500 --> 01:11.500
Just then, the Wunu camp suddenly mobilized troops toward the southern gate, exploiting Yiyang's internal chaos to assault the city and breaching it that very night. Most of the volunteer army scattered like birds and beasts. King of Jin Sikong Yao led his troops to fight to the death, and was personally slain beneath his horse by Shi Lang.
